### ❌ 3 Tests Failing (stale reference bug)

All 3 failures share the same root cause: after `state = DuelEngine.Apply(state, ...)` returns a cloned state, the tests still reference the old `player` variable:

1. **`PlayCard_UsesDiscountedCost`** (line 225) — `player` variable stale after clone
2. **`Aura_StacksThisTurn_MultipleDiscountsAccumulate`** (line 442) — Same stale reference
3. **`Wand_FirstSpellEachTurn_WorksViaFullFlow`** (line 400) — Same

Fix: re-assign `player = state.Players[0]` after each `DuelEngine.Apply` call (already fixed in `PlayCard_ConsumesFirstSpellEachTurn`). Three more occurrences need the same fix in the test file.

